# Kitchen Finks (CR 702.79a, 603.4): it enters on turn 3 and Bot1 gains 2. Bot2 Bolts it on turn 4: it dies with no -1/-1
# counter, so persist returns it - a new object (CR 400.7), with a -1/-1 counter, a 2/1 - and its enters ability gains Bot1
# 2 more. Bolted again on turn 6, it dies with that counter on it (persist's "if it had no -1/-1 counters" reads it as it
# last was, the 2013-06-07 ruling), so it stays in the graveyard.

